# The difference of two balls with one-limb centers: ball_add_1 with the second center negated.
kernel:        ball_sub_1
input:         stored cx
input:         stored rx
input:         stored cy
input:         stored ry
output:        cz
output:        rz
value:         cx-cy
requires:      nonneg rx
requires:      nonneg ry
ensures:       encloses cz rz x-y x=cx,rx y=cy,ry
min_precision: 1
theorem:       proofs/theories/Ball2.v ball_sub_1_correct
source:        midpoint-radius difference (Milestone 1 listing)
license:       algorithm and proof: MIT
status:        proved
entry:         yes
cone_exempt:   the radius never reaches the center; the special states of the ball layer (Milestone 1 statements, Ball kernels) test the center and the radii

n        = neg(cy)
(cz, rz) = ball_add_1(cx, rx, n, ry)
